1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,078
Your car has one radiator.

2
00:00:02,258 --> 00:00:04,371
The Bugatti Veyron has ten.

3
00:00:04,551 --> 00:00:07,606
Not because Bugatti wanted to show off,

4
00:00:07,606 --> 00:00:10,191
but because a car that makes more

5
00:00:10,191 --> 00:00:13,403
than one thousand horsepower turns a huge

6
00:00:13,403 --> 00:00:15,362
amount of fuel into heat,

7
00:00:15,362 --> 00:00:18,025
and that heat has to go somewhere,

8
00:00:18,025 --> 00:00:21,002
or the car destroys itself in minutes.

9
00:00:21,182 --> 00:00:24,173
Today, ten parts of a Bugatti that

10
00:00:24,173 --> 00:00:26,989
exist because of one crazy goal,

11
00:00:26,989 --> 00:00:29,100
and why each one exists.

12
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:31,821
The goal came from Ferdinand Piech,

13
00:00:31,821 --> 00:00:34,192
the head of the Volkswagen Group at

14
00:00:34,192 --> 00:00:36,427
the end of the nineteen nineties.

15
00:00:36,607 --> 00:00:38,795
He wanted a car with more than

16
00:00:38,795 --> 00:00:41,057
one thousand metric horsepower,

17
00:00:41,057 --> 00:00:44,047
a top speed above four hundred kilometres

18
00:00:44,047 --> 00:00:46,528
per hour, and the comfort to drive

19
00:00:46,528 --> 00:00:47,695
it to the opera.

20
00:00:47,875 --> 00:00:50,847
Engineers said it was nearly impossible.

21
00:00:51,027 --> 00:00:54,028
The Veyron arrived in two thousand five,

22
00:00:54,028 --> 00:00:56,354
and every strange part on it is

23
00:00:56,354 --> 00:00:58,155
a solution to that goal.

24
00:00:58,506 --> 00:01:01,516
As always, every fact here comes from

25
00:01:01,516 --> 00:01:02,736
a named source,

26
00:01:02,736 --> 00:01:06,479
Bugatti, Volkswagen and automotive references,

27
00:01:06,479 --> 00:01:08,920
all listed in the description.

28
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:10,644
Let's start with the heat.

29
00:01:10,994 --> 00:01:13,523
Why does a Bugatti Veyron need ten

30
00:01:13,523 --> 00:01:14,268
radiators?

31
00:01:14,448 --> 00:01:17,687
Because of a basic rule of engines.

32
00:01:17,867 --> 00:01:19,678
Only part of the energy in the

33
00:01:19,678 --> 00:01:20,885
fuel becomes motion.

34
00:01:21,065 --> 00:01:22,842
Most of it becomes heat.

35
00:01:23,022 --> 00:01:26,611
For every horsepower that pushes the car

36
00:01:26,611 --> 00:01:30,559
forward, an engine produces even more energy

37
00:01:30,559 --> 00:01:31,276
as heat.

38
00:01:31,456 --> 00:01:32,574
At full power,

39
00:01:32,574 --> 00:01:35,687
the Veyron's engine is producing a huge

40
00:01:35,687 --> 00:01:36,885
amount of heat,

41
00:01:36,885 --> 00:01:40,238
and a normal radiator would be overwhelmed

42
00:01:40,238 --> 00:01:41,116
in seconds.

43
00:01:41,466 --> 00:01:44,623
So the heat is split into separate

44
00:01:44,623 --> 00:01:45,366
systems.

45
00:01:45,546 --> 00:01:48,054
Three radiators cool the engine.

46
00:01:48,234 --> 00:01:50,966
One heat exchanger cools the air coming

47
00:01:50,966 --> 00:01:52,576
from the turbochargers.

48
00:01:52,756 --> 00:01:54,649
Two serve the air conditioning.

49
00:01:54,829 --> 00:01:58,284
And separate coolers handle the engine oil,

50
00:01:58,284 --> 00:01:59,569
the gearbox oil,

51
00:01:59,569 --> 00:02:01,257
the differential oil,

52
00:02:01,257 --> 00:02:04,149
and the hydraulic oil that moves the

53
00:02:04,149 --> 00:02:04,953
rear wing.

54
00:02:05,133 --> 00:02:06,344
Ten in total,

55
00:02:06,344 --> 00:02:09,231
each one sized for its own job.

56
00:02:09,581 --> 00:02:12,271
That is why the Veyron is covered

57
00:02:12,271 --> 00:02:13,249
in openings.

58
00:02:13,429 --> 00:02:15,228
The big horseshoe grille,

59
00:02:15,228 --> 00:02:17,027
the intakes in the front,

60
00:02:17,027 --> 00:02:19,330
the openings on the sides and on

61
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:19,977
the roof.

62
00:02:20,157 --> 00:02:21,748
They are not decoration.

63
00:02:21,928 --> 00:02:24,204
They are the mouths that feed air

64
00:02:24,204 --> 00:02:25,376
to the radiators.

65
00:02:25,556 --> 00:02:28,015
A Bugatti at full speed is as

66
00:02:28,015 --> 00:02:30,643
much a cooling machine as it is

67
00:02:30,643 --> 00:02:31,152
a car.

68
00:02:31,502 --> 00:02:34,168
Why does a Bugatti have an engine

69
00:02:34,168 --> 00:02:35,461
shaped like a W?

70
00:02:35,641 --> 00:02:39,147
To fit sixteen cylinders into a short

71
00:02:39,147 --> 00:02:39,716
space.

72
00:02:39,896 --> 00:02:42,642
A V sixteen would have been very

73
00:02:42,642 --> 00:02:45,303
long, and a long engine makes a

74
00:02:45,303 --> 00:02:46,676
long, heavy car.

75
00:02:46,856 --> 00:02:50,042
Instead, the W sixteen is like two

76
00:02:50,042 --> 00:02:53,884
narrow V eight engines joined together at

77
00:02:53,884 --> 00:02:54,727
an angle.

78
00:02:54,907 --> 00:02:56,710
Seen from the front,

79
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:59,685
the four rows of cylinders form a

80
00:02:59,685 --> 00:02:59,865
W.

81
00:03:00,215 --> 00:03:03,568
The idea came from Volkswagen's VR six

82
00:03:03,568 --> 00:03:06,744
engine, which put six cylinders in a

83
00:03:06,744 --> 00:03:09,656
very narrow V so they could share

84
00:03:09,656 --> 00:03:11,244
one cylinder head.

85
00:03:11,424 --> 00:03:15,198
Bugatti's engineers took two of those narrow

86
00:03:15,198 --> 00:03:18,715
blocks and joined them on one crankshaft.

87
00:03:18,895 --> 00:03:21,718
The result is an eight litre engine

88
00:03:21,718 --> 00:03:25,347
with sixteen cylinders and sixty-four valves,

89
00:03:25,347 --> 00:03:27,525
about as long as a normal V

90
00:03:27,525 --> 00:03:28,009
eight.

91
00:03:28,359 --> 00:03:31,280
More cylinders means more power from the

92
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,595
same engine speed,

93
00:03:32,595 --> 00:03:34,129
and smoother running.

94
00:03:34,309 --> 00:03:36,713
The W sixteen gave the Veyron its

95
00:03:36,713 --> 00:03:40,065
thousand horsepower, and later versions in the

96
00:03:40,065 --> 00:03:43,562
Chiron produced around fifteen hundred and more.

97
00:03:43,742 --> 00:03:45,855
It is one of the most complex

98
00:03:45,855 --> 00:03:47,968
production engines ever made,

99
00:03:47,968 --> 00:03:49,790
and it is also one of the

100
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:52,705
reasons the car needs so many radiators.

101
00:03:53,055 --> 00:03:55,674
Why does the Bugatti engine have four

102
00:03:55,674 --> 00:03:56,665
turbochargers?

103
00:03:56,845 --> 00:03:59,452
A turbo uses the exhaust gas to

104
00:03:59,452 --> 00:04:02,396
spin a turbine that pushes more air

105
00:04:02,396 --> 00:04:03,742
into the engine.

106
00:04:03,922 --> 00:04:06,491
More air means more fuel can burn,

107
00:04:06,491 --> 00:04:07,625
and more power.

108
00:04:07,805 --> 00:04:10,161
But one huge turbo would be slow

109
00:04:10,161 --> 00:04:10,824
to react.

110
00:04:11,004 --> 00:04:13,585
Four smaller turbos respond faster,

111
00:04:13,585 --> 00:04:15,946
and they can be shared among the

112
00:04:15,946 --> 00:04:17,273
sixteen cylinders.

113
00:04:17,624 --> 00:04:18,786
On the Chiron,

114
00:04:18,786 --> 00:04:22,024
Bugatti made the turbos work in stages.

115
00:04:22,204 --> 00:04:23,926
At low engine speed,

116
00:04:23,926 --> 00:04:26,251
only two turbos are active,

117
00:04:26,251 --> 00:04:28,921
so they spin up quickly and the

118
00:04:28,921 --> 00:04:31,074
car responds immediately.

119
00:04:31,254 --> 00:04:32,753
At higher speed,

120
00:04:32,753 --> 00:04:34,815
the other two join in,

121
00:04:34,815 --> 00:04:37,813
and all four deliver full power.

122
00:04:37,993 --> 00:04:40,585
The driver feels a smooth,

123
00:04:40,585 --> 00:04:44,472
endless push, instead of a sudden kick.

124
00:04:44,822 --> 00:04:46,675
Turbos also add heat,

125
00:04:46,675 --> 00:04:49,942
because compressing air makes it hot.

126
00:04:50,122 --> 00:04:52,444
Hot air is less dense and makes

127
00:04:52,444 --> 00:04:53,268
less power.

128
00:04:53,448 --> 00:04:55,514
That is why the Bugatti has a

129
00:04:55,514 --> 00:04:58,363
system to cool the compressed air before

130
00:04:58,363 --> 00:04:59,859
it enters the engine,

131
00:04:59,859 --> 00:05:01,853
with its own heat exchanger.

132
00:05:02,033 --> 00:05:03,821
One more radiator.

133
00:05:04,001 --> 00:05:07,151
Every part that adds power also adds

134
00:05:07,151 --> 00:05:07,589
heat.

135
00:05:07,939 --> 00:05:10,269
Why does the Bugatti Veyron have two

136
00:05:10,269 --> 00:05:11,758
scoops behind the roof?

137
00:05:11,938 --> 00:05:13,761
They feed air to the engine.

138
00:05:13,941 --> 00:05:17,143
The W sixteen breathes an enormous amount

139
00:05:17,143 --> 00:05:18,782
of air at full power.

140
00:05:18,962 --> 00:05:21,128
The air on the roof is clean

141
00:05:21,128 --> 00:05:23,526
and fast, away from the hot air

142
00:05:23,526 --> 00:05:25,615
and dirt around the wheels.

143
00:05:25,795 --> 00:05:27,944
The scoops catch it and send it

144
00:05:27,944 --> 00:05:30,787
straight down to the engine's air intake.

145
00:05:31,138 --> 00:05:32,687
On a mid engined car,

146
00:05:32,687 --> 00:05:35,933
the engine sits right behind the passengers,

147
00:05:35,933 --> 00:05:37,778
and air has to find a way

148
00:05:37,778 --> 00:05:37,999
in.

149
00:05:38,179 --> 00:05:40,851
Many supercars use side intakes,

150
00:05:40,851 --> 00:05:43,607
but the roof scoops on the Veyron

151
00:05:43,607 --> 00:05:44,776
give a direct,

152
00:05:44,776 --> 00:05:46,863
short path to the engine.

153
00:05:47,043 --> 00:05:48,260
At high speed,

154
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:51,475
the moving air even pushes itself in,

155
00:05:51,475 --> 00:05:55,124
like a gentle supercharger called ram air.

156
00:05:55,474 --> 00:05:58,139
Bugatti says that at full power,

157
00:05:58,139 --> 00:06:01,221
its W sixteen engines swallow tens of

158
00:06:01,221 --> 00:06:04,553
thousands of litres of air every minute.

159
00:06:04,733 --> 00:06:06,791
That is more air than a person

160
00:06:06,791 --> 00:06:08,506
breathes in several days.

161
00:06:08,686 --> 00:06:11,036
The scoops on the roof are the

162
00:06:11,036 --> 00:06:13,464
open mouth of that giant set of

163
00:06:13,464 --> 00:06:13,934
lungs.

164
00:06:14,284 --> 00:06:15,947
Why does the rear wing of a

165
00:06:15,947 --> 00:06:17,918
Bugatti stand up when it brakes?

166
00:06:18,098 --> 00:06:19,409
It is an airbrake.

167
00:06:19,589 --> 00:06:21,978
Under hard braking at high speed,

168
00:06:21,978 --> 00:06:23,643
the wing tilts steeply,

169
00:06:23,643 --> 00:06:25,743
like a wall against the wind.

170
00:06:25,923 --> 00:06:27,546
The air pushes on it,

171
00:06:27,546 --> 00:06:29,864
adding a lot of braking force,

172
00:06:29,864 --> 00:06:32,105
and it pushes the rear of the

173
00:06:32,105 --> 00:06:34,501
car down, so the rear tyres can

174
00:06:34,501 --> 00:06:35,814
brake harder too.

175
00:06:36,165 --> 00:06:39,609
Stopping from more than four hundred kilometres

176
00:06:39,609 --> 00:06:41,807
per hour is one of the hardest

177
00:06:41,807 --> 00:06:42,980
jobs on the car.

178
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:45,876
The brakes turn the car's energy into

179
00:06:45,876 --> 00:06:48,371
heat, and at that speed the amount

180
00:06:48,371 --> 00:06:49,986
of energy is enormous.

181
00:06:50,166 --> 00:06:51,873
The airbrake shares the work.

182
00:06:52,053 --> 00:06:54,116
It also stabilises the car,

183
00:06:54,116 --> 00:06:57,554
because heavy braking normally makes the rear

184
00:06:57,554 --> 00:06:59,158
go light and nervous.

185
00:06:59,509 --> 00:07:01,921
The wing moves with hydraulics,

186
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:04,878
and it changes its angle for different

187
00:07:04,878 --> 00:07:05,267
jobs.

188
00:07:05,447 --> 00:07:06,966
Low for top speed,

189
00:07:06,966 --> 00:07:08,653
higher for handling,

190
00:07:08,653 --> 00:07:10,509
and steep for braking.

191
00:07:10,689 --> 00:07:14,265
The hydraulic oil gets its own radiator,

192
00:07:14,265 --> 00:07:15,159
of course.

193
00:07:15,339 --> 00:07:16,452
On a Bugatti,

194
00:07:16,452 --> 00:07:19,449
even the wing has a cooling system.

195
00:07:19,799 --> 00:07:22,344
Why would a Bugatti Veyron run out

196
00:07:22,344 --> 00:07:24,890
of fuel in about twelve minutes at

197
00:07:24,890 --> 00:07:25,638
top speed?

198
00:07:25,818 --> 00:07:27,512
Because at full power,

199
00:07:27,512 --> 00:07:30,437
the engine burns fuel at an incredible

200
00:07:30,437 --> 00:07:30,822
rate.

201
00:07:31,002 --> 00:07:33,967
The Veyron's tank holds about one hundred

202
00:07:33,967 --> 00:07:34,474
litres.

203
00:07:34,654 --> 00:07:35,688
At top speed,

204
00:07:35,688 --> 00:07:38,076
the engine would use all of it

205
00:07:38,076 --> 00:07:40,146
in roughly twelve minutes,

206
00:07:40,146 --> 00:07:42,932
according to Bugatti's own figures.

207
00:07:43,282 --> 00:07:45,511
That is the price of power.

208
00:07:45,691 --> 00:07:47,937
Every horsepower needs fuel,

209
00:07:47,937 --> 00:07:50,985
and a thousand horsepower needs a fire

210
00:07:50,985 --> 00:07:51,867
hose of it.

211
00:07:52,047 --> 00:07:53,601
In normal driving,

212
00:07:53,601 --> 00:07:56,623
the Veyron is much more reasonable,

213
00:07:56,623 --> 00:07:58,177
but still thirsty.

214
00:07:58,357 --> 00:08:01,163
The fuel system has multiple pumps to

215
00:08:01,163 --> 00:08:02,680
keep the engine fed,

216
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:06,624
even under strong acceleration and cornering forces.

217
00:08:06,974 --> 00:08:10,843
Twelve minutes at top speed sounds dramatic,

218
00:08:10,843 --> 00:08:14,185
but in reality it is almost impossible

219
00:08:14,185 --> 00:08:16,912
to stay at top speed that long.

220
00:08:17,092 --> 00:08:19,557
No public road and very few test

221
00:08:19,557 --> 00:08:21,329
tracks are long enough.

222
00:08:21,509 --> 00:08:24,857
The tyres are also designed for limited

223
00:08:24,857 --> 00:08:26,745
time at maximum speed.

224
00:08:26,925 --> 00:08:27,880
The fuel tank,

225
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,197
the tyres and the cooling were all

226
00:08:30,197 --> 00:08:32,856
designed around the same few minutes of

227
00:08:32,856 --> 00:08:33,810
extreme speed.

228
00:08:34,161 --> 00:08:36,563
Why is the Bugatti grille shaped like

229
00:08:36,563 --> 00:08:37,342
a horseshoe?

230
00:08:37,522 --> 00:08:40,109
It is a tradition from the original

231
00:08:40,109 --> 00:08:43,436
Bugatti company, founded by Ettore Bugatti in

232
00:08:43,436 --> 00:08:46,171
Molsheim, France, in nineteen o nine.

233
00:08:46,351 --> 00:08:49,500
His classic cars carried a radiator shaped

234
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:50,774
like a horseshoe,

235
00:08:50,774 --> 00:08:52,949
and it became the face of the

236
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:53,398
brand.

237
00:08:53,578 --> 00:08:55,529
Ettore was a lover of horses,

238
00:08:55,529 --> 00:08:57,682
and the shape became part of the

239
00:08:57,682 --> 00:08:58,153
legend.

240
00:08:58,503 --> 00:09:00,184
On the modern Bugatti,

241
00:09:00,184 --> 00:09:02,705
the horseshoe is not just a logo.

242
00:09:02,885 --> 00:09:04,537
It is a real air intake,

243
00:09:04,537 --> 00:09:07,497
feeding cooling air to the radiators behind

244
00:09:07,497 --> 00:09:07,704
it.

245
00:09:07,884 --> 00:09:10,608
The designers had to make the brand's

246
00:09:10,608 --> 00:09:13,553
most famous shape work as an engineering

247
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:13,921
part.

248
00:09:14,101 --> 00:09:16,541
Its size and position were tuned with

249
00:09:16,541 --> 00:09:18,651
the rest of the front intakes to

250
00:09:18,651 --> 00:09:21,222
feed the cooling system at four hundred

251
00:09:21,222 --> 00:09:22,541
kilometres per hour.

252
00:09:22,892 --> 00:09:26,062
The Bugatti Type thirty-five of the nineteen

253
00:09:26,062 --> 00:09:28,800
twenties, with its horseshoe radiator,

254
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:31,466
was one of the most successful racing

255
00:09:31,466 --> 00:09:32,618
cars in history,

256
00:09:32,618 --> 00:09:35,140
winning more than a thousand races.

257
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:37,960
When Volkswagen revived the brand,

258
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:40,367
keeping that shape was a way of

259
00:09:40,367 --> 00:09:43,317
connecting the new hypercar to the old

260
00:09:43,317 --> 00:09:44,016
champion.

261
00:09:44,196 --> 00:09:46,901
One shape, a hundred years apart.

262
00:09:47,251 --> 00:09:49,835
Why does the Bugatti Chiron have a

263
00:09:49,835 --> 00:09:52,115
giant curved line on its side?

264
00:09:52,295 --> 00:09:54,599
It is called the Bugatti line,

265
00:09:54,599 --> 00:09:55,674
or the C line.

266
00:09:55,854 --> 00:09:58,543
It looks like a pure design signature,

267
00:09:58,543 --> 00:10:00,312
sweeping around the door.

268
00:10:00,492 --> 00:10:02,535
But it is also an air channel.

269
00:10:02,715 --> 00:10:05,380
The curve guides air into the intakes

270
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:08,044
that feed the engine and the coolers.

271
00:10:08,395 --> 00:10:12,248
The Chiron makes about fifteen hundred horsepower,

272
00:10:12,248 --> 00:10:14,868
half again as much as the original

273
00:10:14,868 --> 00:10:15,407
Veyron.

274
00:10:15,587 --> 00:10:18,176
More power meant even more heat,

275
00:10:18,176 --> 00:10:20,846
so the designers needed more air.

276
00:10:21,026 --> 00:10:23,244
Instead of adding more holes,

277
00:10:23,244 --> 00:10:25,844
they built a giant intake into the

278
00:10:25,844 --> 00:10:28,062
most visible line of the car.

279
00:10:28,242 --> 00:10:30,628
The style and the cooling are the

280
00:10:30,628 --> 00:10:31,423
same thing.

281
00:10:31,773 --> 00:10:34,969
This is a theme across all Bugatti

282
00:10:34,969 --> 00:10:35,627
design.

283
00:10:35,807 --> 00:10:38,360
Almost every surface has to do a

284
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,636
job for the air,

285
00:10:39,636 --> 00:10:42,428
whether it is pushing the car down,

286
00:10:42,428 --> 00:10:43,944
feeding a radiator,

287
00:10:43,944 --> 00:10:45,699
or cooling the brakes.

288
00:10:45,879 --> 00:10:48,531
The designers like to say that form

289
00:10:48,531 --> 00:10:50,047
follows performance.

290
00:10:50,227 --> 00:10:51,659
On a car this fast,

291
00:10:51,659 --> 00:10:53,769
there is no space for a line

292
00:10:53,769 --> 00:10:55,126
